 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the election law, in relation to increasing the number of\nregistrants an election district may contain with the approval of the county\nboard of elections; authorizes increase of county committee",
    "basePrintNo": "S6855",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6855-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§4-100 & 2-104, El L",
    "lawSection": "Election Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6855\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the election law, in relation to increasing the number\nof registrants an election district may contain with the approval of the\ncounty board of elections; authorizes increase of county committee\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would raise the election district registrant enrollment from a\nMaximum of 1,150 registrants to 2,000.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend Election Law § 4-100(3) (a) revises\nthe definition of an \"election districts\" to expand its maximum regis-\ntrants from eleven hundred fifty to two thousand.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would amend subdivision one of § 2-104 of Election\nlaw to provide for additional party county committee member represen-\ntation within expanded election districts.\n\nSection 3 of the bill provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUpon enactment this legislation would raise the limit of voters allowed\nin every election district from 1,150 voters to 2,000. The current\nelection district registrant enrollment limits were prescribed based on\nthe fact that the old lever voter machines were not capable of handling\nmore than 1,000 votes per election; thus, a strict limit of 1,150 voters\nper district was necessary. The optical scanners will read and hold up\nto approximately 4,000 ballots/voters per machine. Therefore, this\nchange in the law aims to serve as mandate relief to municipalities by\nallowing them to consolidate districts and reduce costs Jr many areas,\nincluding hiring fewer election inspectors; fewer ballots to order; and\nrequiring less time testing ballots.\n\nAdditionally, this bill provides for additional county party committee\nrepresentation to accommodate an increase in size of an election\ndistricts.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020: A.6093 Passed Assembly / S.546 Died in Elections\n\n2019:A.6093 Remained in election law/ S.546 Passed Senate\n\n2018:A.5576 Passed Assembly / S.2794 Third Reading calendar\n\n2017:A.5576 Passed Assembly / S.2794 Third Reading calendar\n\n2016:A.4189 Passed Assembly / S.7072 Third Reading calendar\n\n2015:A.4189 Third Reading calendar /S.3285 Third Reading calendar\n2014:A.6856 Third Reading calendar /S.3285 Third Reading calendar\n\n2013:A.6856 Third reading calendar /5.3285 - Died in Rules\n\n2012:A.10434 Died in Rules/5.7466- Died in Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n",
